From 2442df30ba2862caa348d76192728e9eabd0f1f7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 9 Oct 2026 22:09:51 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(facts): the owner's corrected job shows, even over a
 contact's old Ally profile (4226)

Tester 48549, on the founder's account (D742): for two contacts who have
an old Ally account, the owner saved a new occupation and employer (saved:
true), marked the old ones wrong, and search still showed the old employer
and title, while get_contact_facts showed neither.

Two causes:
- The search rows take employer and job title from the contact's own
  "User" row (the old Ally profile), and applyFacts let a saved fact fill
  only an empty field. So the profile always won. Now the owner's OWN saved
  fact wins over that profile. A fact somebody else made public still only
  fills an empty field.
- correct_contact_fact retracts the owner's old row, and the next save of
  that field upserted onto the same row (the unique index includes
  retracted rows) without clearing retracted_at. It reported saved and
  stayed invisible. The upsert now clears the retraction: a new value is
  the owner's new word.

The first case of 48549 (one contact in the phone that no search finds)
needs the number resolved from its export hash on the server. That is left
for daytime.

DONE WHEN: on a fictional seat, a contact with an ally_account profile gets
a corrected occupation and employer; search and get_contact_facts show the
new values (2 of 2).

